 "intro": "Near Zela in Pontus, 67 BC. While Lucullus campaigned in Armenia, Mithridates has returned to Pontus with a new army. You are Gaius Valerius Triarius, Lucullus’s legate. The sources are brief.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s and Plutarch’s accounts, Triarius, perhaps hoping to win before Lucullus arrived, fought Mithridates near Zela and was badly beaten: about 7,000 Romans died, including 24 tribunes and 150 centurions. Mithridates was wounded by a Roman centurion who had slipped among his men, which halted the pursuit. Lucullus arrived to find the dead unburied, and his mutinous army would not fight. Pompey soon replaced him. The other choices are what-ifs.",
